    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it’s not just a \"low moment\" though. a low moment implies it'll go back up. this feels different. it feels like the light has actually been extinguished. i look at my old work and i don't even recognize the person who made it. it’s like i'm a ghost haunting my own life. how do you even keep going when you realize the thing that made you \"you\" is just... permanently gone?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When everything feels fundamentally changed, it's important to shift the focus from \"what I used to be\" to \"who I am right now.\" Instead of fighting the feeling that the old self is gone, try exploring what interests you in this new space, even if it feels small or unrecognizable. Small, tiny acts of self-compassion—like noticing a good color in the sky or listening to a song without expectation—can gently begin to reignite a quiet spark. You have depth within you, even if it feels buried under exhaustion right now.",
      "source": "target",
